Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Compose opaque GDI children over per-pixel parents.

Photoshop's Type Context Bar hosts standard Edit controls initialized with
LWA_ALPHA=255 inside an UpdateLayeredWindow popup. Their buffers contain the
font and size, but they inherit the parent's dummy GDI surface and empty clip.
Removing WS_EX_LAYERED from the edits does not fix that inherited surface.

Give these opaque layered children offscreen GDI caches when they have a
per-pixel ancestor. Clip independently surfaced children against ancestor
geometry instead of their parent's dummy surface. Mark affected ancestors so
normal window trees keep their existing painting path, and refresh presentation
when a control or its container moves, hides or is destroyed. Also initialize
children when the parent's first per-pixel update follows their creation.

Snapshot window metadata and referenced child caches before locking a drawing
surface: window position updates take the user lock before the surface lock.
No window-tree queries run while composing pixels. A scaled target defers its
presentation callbacks to the outer surface after that surface is unlocked.

Compose visible cached controls from back to front into a temporary copy at
presentation time. Consume that copy once in the scaling path. On X11 use a
temporary non-SHM XImage for these composed pixels: copying them into the shared
XImage would overwrite the application's backing bitmap and leave stale controls
behind after a move or hide. The application's per-pixel source stays intact.

This supports opaque LWA_ALPHA-only child controls, not general semi-transparent
or color-keyed child-window composition. Existing non-layered controls, ordinary
parents and unsupported alpha modes keep their previous drawing paths. There
are no application-class checks, preference changes or compositor rules.

Reproducer: tests/layered/context-controls.c. Pixel checks cover nonempty text,
text changes, parent updates, resizing, control/container movement and visibility,
destruction, and concurrent GDI painting/control movement. Both creation orders pass under Xvfb and KWin/XWayland; a
separate disposable-prefix Xvfb run also passes at 144 DPI. Photoshop's font,
size editing and focus-switch workflow was confirmed in an isolated runtime.

